Failed-syscall tracer (sweetsyserr): print the command of a failed ioctl, fsctl and ffsctl and count each command
once. ffsctl had no name and no detail, and all its failures of one process collapsed into a single "(245) e=25"
line, so after 1145 the remaining APFS query that HFS answers with ENOTTY in LocalStorageFileProvider's lookup of a
file (Safari's .download placeholder) could not be named. Also correct the comment: names are matched against
proc_selfname() (p_name, 31 characters here), not p_comm, so list full names.

diff --git a/bsd/kern/sweet_amfi.c b/bsd/kern/sweet_amfi.c
--- a/bsd/kern/sweet_amfi.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/sweet_amfi.c
@@ -637,8 +637,10 @@
  *
  *   SWEET ERR: containermanagerd[41] mkdir(136) e=45 "/private/var/containers/Data/System/..."
  *
- * Names are compared against p_comm (16 characters: containermanagerd_system shows as
- * "containermanager"). At most SWEET_SYSERR_MAX lines in total.
+ * Names are compared against proc_selfname() (p_name, at most 31 characters here, else p_comm): a listed name
+ * matches exactly, or as a longer name whose first 31 characters are it, so list full names
+ * ("com.apple.DocumentManagerCore.Downloads"). ioctl/fsctl/ffsctl print their command and count once per command.
+ * At most SWEET_SYSERR_MAX lines in total.
  */
